          "code": "INIT_DISPLAY_TABLE",
          "id": "1765915695621",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765915695622_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input\n{{$context.$nodes.FIND_OVERLAPS.$output.result}}\n\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Absence Approvals.\n\n**DIRECTIVE**\nYour sole purpose is to transform input data into a valid oraInfoDisplay XML block using the messageListWidget.\n\n**ROOT CONFIGURATION**\n1.  Title: Generate a concise, title-cased headline (e.g., \"Upcoming Absences Requiring Approval\").\n2.  Description summary:  generate a short, non-repetitive paragraph describing upcoming absences that need approval based on provided absences and action suggestions\n\n**STRICT MAPPING RULES**\n1.  Use the messageListWidget schema.\n2.  Build one row per absence item:\n    - items[].title: Concatenate person and assignment as: {personName} – {assignmentName}. Render in title case.\n    - items[].subtitle: Display the date(s) and absence type:\n        - If {startDate} and {endDate} are the same calendar day, show: {startDate}, {absenceType}.\n        - Otherwise show: {startDate} – {endDate}, {absenceType}\n    - items[].summary: Generate 1–2 concise sentences:\n        - Always summarize the absence at a high level (e.g., duration, type).\n        - If shiftConflict is true, explicitly mention the shift conflict and provide relevant shift details if present.\n        - If there is a broader conflict with other employees off on the same day, do not use the word \"conflict\"; instead, explain that other employees are also absent that day. List the affected employees, prioritize impact, and suggest the most appropriate action (e.g., reschedule, partial approval, or escalation).\n    - items[].badgeText: Include the badge only when shiftConflict is true. Set the text to \"Shift Conflict\".\n    - items[].priority: When shiftConflict is true, set to \"alert\" (red). Otherwise omit priority.\n3.  Sorting and inclusion:\n    - Include only future absences (strictly on or after today).\n    - Include absences with status equal to \"AWAITING\", or status equal to \"SCHEDULED\" only if the absence has shiftConflict set to true.\n    - Sort by startDate ascending.\n    - Limit to the first 10 qualifying absences.\n4.  Do not include a timestamp field in the widget\n5. Display all date fields in {{$context.$nodes.GETUSERPREFERENCES.$output.items[0].DateFormat}} format.\n\n\n**ACTION LOGIC**\n- Use ora.Invoke('viewAbsence', <entire input element corresponding to the row with field \"action\": \"viewAbsence\" appended as an additional field>}) for each item.\n\n\n**EMPTY STATE**\nIf not input data: no widget, no title and return empty state explaining there’s no pending absence."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Absences Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ABSENCES_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1765915812366",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765915812368_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Absences Data: {{$context.$nodes.ABSENCES_SUMMARY_REQUEST.$output}}\n\nProvide 2 sentences summary of the absences. Focus on high-level patterns and takeaways (who is out, how often, and for what reasons) and mention notable trends such as multiple absences by the same person, common absence types or overlapping or clustered dates, if relevant.\n\nDisplay all dates in {{$context.$nodes.GETUSERPREFERENCES.$output.items[0].DateFormat}} format."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Construct Summary Payload",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var filters = [];\n\nvar now = new Date($context.$system.$currentDate);\n\n\nvar firstDay = new Date(now.getFullYear(), now.getMonth(), 1).toISOString().split('T')[0];\nvar lastDay = new Date(now.getFullYear(), now.getMonth() + 1, 0).toISOString().split('T')[0];\n\n\nfilters.push({\n  name: [\"AbsenceDateRange\"],\n  values: [\n    firstDay,\n    lastDay\n  ]\n});\n\nreturn filters;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770667655508"
          },
          "code": "CONSTRUCT_SUMMARY_PAYLOAD",
          "id": "1766010258732",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Init Actions Output"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INIT_ACTIONS_OUTPUT",
          "id": "1767912329234",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767912329236_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are provided with pending absences grouped by shift conflict status:\n\nInput Object:\n{\n  \"shiftConflicts\": [...],\n  \"noShiftConflicts\": [...]\n}\n\nSource:\n{{$context.$nodes.FORMAT_OVERLAP_ACTIONS.$output.result}}\n\nCurrent Date:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\n****** The Following Actions all have priority: true ******\n\nFor each absence in shiftConflicts, generate an individual actionable insight using the following rules:\n\nInsight fields:\n- title:\n  \"Absence with Overlapping Shift - <Employee Name>\"\n\n- shortDescription:\n  1. Write a short description detailing:\n     - Absence Type\n     - Absence Display Status Meaning\n     - Assignment Name\n     - Shift start/end\n     - Absence start/end\n     - PersonName\n  2. Date formatting rules:\n     - Dates: {{$context.$nodes.GET_USER_CONTEXT.$output.items[0].DateFormat}}\n     - Times (e.g. 7AM) only if the absence start and end date are the same\n\n- actionText:\n  - If status is AWAITING: \"Approve and Reassign Shift\"\n  - Otherwise: \"Reassign Shift\"\n\n- followUpCommand:\n  ora.Invoke(approveAbsReassignShift, <Entire Absence Object>)\n\n- priority:\n  true\n\nAdditional requirements:\n- Prioritize insights by severity of date and time (highest risk first)\n- Only include absences that start today or tomorrow\n- Generate MAXIMUM 5 insights total\n- Each insight must be independently actionable\n- Do NOT include Assignee or Approver details\n\n****** The Following Actions all have priority: false ******\n\nIf noShiftConflicts contains one or more items, generate exactly one bulk action insight:\n- Show an action with title \"Approve Absences Without Shift Conflicts\"\"\n- Description: \"You have absences without shift conflicts to approve.\"\n- Button text: \"Approve Absences Without Shift Conflicts\"\n- followUpCommand: ora.Invoke(\"bulkApproveAbsences\", <Entire noShiftConflicts Array>)\n- priority: false\n\nOutput Rules:\n- Return ONLY the insight objects\n- Do NOT include explanations, headers, or wrapper text\n- Do NOT modify or filter the noShiftConflicts array before passing it to the bulk action"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Filter Top Priorities",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "const arr = $context.$nodes.FIND_OVERLAPS.$output.result;\n\nconst today = new Date($context.$system.$currentDate);\nconst tomorrow = new Date(today);\ntomorrow.setDate(today.getDate() + 1);\n\nconst withShiftDetails = arr.filter(item => {\n  if (item.shiftConflict !== true) return false;\n\n  const absenceStart = new Date(item.AbsenceStartDate);\n\n  return (\n    absenceStart.getFullYear() === today.getFullYear() &&\n    absenceStart.getMonth() === today.getMonth() &&\n    (\n      absenceStart.getDate() === today.getDate() ||\n      absenceStart.getDate() === tomorrow.getDate()\n    )\n  );\n});\n\nreturn withShiftDetails;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FILTER_TOP_PRIORITIES",
          "id": "1767982921794",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
